(Bug #69 in the call form LANGUAGE.md:419 documents - `<function> of each
 <var> from <collection> treating <match> as <replacement>`. The tag the
 clause hands the `value` parameter has to be the element's own, or the
 replacement's when the substitution fires, whichever the runtime found.)

To announce with a value called what.
  print what.

a value called probe is "a".
announce of each item from [1, "a"] treating probe as "b".

a value called nine is 9.
announce of each item from [1, "a"] treating "a" as nine.

(And the other direction: a `value` PARAMETER used as the clause's match,
 whose tag is read from the frame it was passed into.)
To swapin with a value called m.
  print each item from [1, "-"] treating m as "X".

a value called dash is "-".
swapin of dash.
a value called seven is 7.
swapin of seven.

(And a `value` replacement over a list whose element type IS static: the tag
 that travels with the argument has to be the replacement's runtime one, not
 the collection's static text - which is what stops 9 being read as a
 pointer inside the callee.)
a list called names is ["ann", "-"].
announce of each name from names treating "-" as nine.
